1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,280
(Leonard:)Fine. Assuming
that everything you say is true...

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,330
(Leonard:)...how does the biologically superior
Homo novus get to work...

3
00:00:06,495 --> 00:00:08,285
(Leonard:)...tomorrow morning?

4
00:00:08,789 --> 00:00:11,079
(Sheldon:)Homo novus doesn't know.

5
00:00:12,042 --> 00:00:14,122
(Leonard:)Well, hang in there.

6
00:00:14,294 --> 00:00:16,794
(Leonard:)Maybe you'll evolve into something
with wings.

7
00:00:28,308 --> 00:00:29,848
SHELDON: Good morning, gentlemen.
- Hey.

8
00:00:30,018 --> 00:00:31,938
(Sheldon:)Good morning.

9
00:00:32,979 --> 00:00:36,319
(Raj:)Is there some new kind of Casual Friday
I don't know about?

10
00:00:36,775 --> 00:00:38,525
(Leonard:)No, he lives here now.

11
00:00:39,402 --> 00:00:40,442
(Howard:)Really? Why?

12
00:00:40,612 --> 00:00:43,702
(Leonard:)Well, since he won't take the bus
and he's too evolved to drive...

13
00:00:43,865 --> 00:00:45,695
...he decided to sleep in his office...

14
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:49,287
(Leonard:)...and shower in the radiation lab
until I'm finished with my experiment.

15
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:53,290
(Raj:)But you finished your experiment
a week ago.

16
00:00:56,962 --> 00:00:58,292
(Leonard:)Yep.

17
00:01:09,182 --> 00:01:12,062
[IN SPANISH]

18
00:01:21,778 --> 00:01:23,068
[LOUD BANGING]

19
00:01:27,951 --> 00:01:29,871
[SPEAKS IN SPANISH]

20
00:01:30,036 --> 00:01:33,126
(Sheldon:)You saw nothing.

